/*
For INSTALL_DT = '2023-01-01':
  • Q1 will compute the installs as COUNT(DISTINCT PLAYER_ID) = 2.
    The numerator (SUM of CASE) for player 1 will add 1 for each matching day1 record (total 2) and for player 2 will add 1 (total 1), so the retention value becomes ROUND((2+1)/2,2) = 1.50.
  • Q2, by contrast, because of its LEFT JOIN only matches at most one row per player (or is expected to, if duplicates were collapsed) would ideally count 1 for player 1 and 1 for player 2, yielding ROUND((1+1)/2,2) = 1.00.
Thus the two queries yield different results under this (hypothetical) situation.
*/

