counterexample:
-- No INSERT statements can differentiate Q1 and Q2 because they are semantically equivalent under the given schema.
-- For example, consider the following test data, which when inserted produces identical results for both queries:

INSERT INTO CUSTOMERS (ID, NAME) VALUES (1, 'Alice');
INSERT INTO CUSTOMERS (ID, NAME) VALUES (2, 'Bob');

INSERT INTO ORDERS (ID, CUSTOMERID) VALUES (1, '1');
-- In this data, Alice has an order so she is excluded, while Bob (with no order) appears in both queries.

